  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{xy}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous for all values of $x$ and $y.$ So,  we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(-2,4)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy}=\\sqrt{(-2)\\cdot 4}=\\sqrt[3]{-8}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
